# Secrets. Deliberately not anchored with a leading slash: that would cover the repository
# root only, and --env=<file> resolves relative to the package, so an environment file can
# legitimately sit in a subdirectory. This holds while environment files are named .env or
# .env.<something> - --env= will load any file you point it at, and one named otherwise is
# not covered here.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
